    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "τB×fF((p,x),(q,y)) := supL(γ) where the sup is w.r.t. all future directed causal curves γ that connect (p,x) and (q,y). If there is no such curve, one sets τ((p,x),(q,y)) = 0. τB×fF satisﬁes the reverse △-inequality"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 10,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 126.719, 553.407, 485.301, 591.741 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "τB×fF((p,x),(q,y)) ≥ τB×fF((p,x),(r,z)) + τB×fF((r,z),(q,y)). For all (p,x),(q,y),(r,z) ∈ I × F. In the following we write also τB×fF = τ."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 11,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 138.599, 547.713, 416.181, 558.622 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "The time seperation function has the following properties:"
