      "font" : "CMSY10",
      "font size" : 10.909,
      "text color" : "[0.0]",
      "content" : "• −I ×f F has the push-up property: if (s,x) ≪ (t,y) if and only if there exists a future directed causal curve from (s,x) to (t,y) with positive length. Moreover I+/−((s,x)) is open for all (s,t) ∈ I × F.",
